      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-216814",
      ":question/problem": "Prove that the function $f: Q \u2192 Q \\cdot Q$ defined by $f(x) = (x, 2x)$ is **NOT** surjective.\n\nA function $f: X \u2192 Y$ is a surjection if {{field-1}}\n\n$f(x) \\ne y$ {{field-2}}\n\nWe can write this formally as follows:\n\n$\u2203x \u2208 X, \u2200y \u2208 Y, f(x) = y$ {{field-3}}\n\nThe negation of this statement is\n\n$\u2200y \u2208 Y, \u2203x \u2208 X, f(x) \\ne y$ {{field-4}}"
